# Exhaustive match on nominal variant type produces zero warnings
# This is the happy path — all constructors are covered.
# ADT constructor scoping: [type Shape [Circle r: Int] [Square s: Int]] injects
# Circle, Square, and Shape as callable unit-variant constructors.
# [Circle r: 5] creates Variant(Circle, Int(5)); match extracts r=5; area = 3*5*5 = 75.
# The outer dict result includes the injected constructor bindings and the area: Int(75) field.
[
  [type Shape
    [Circle r: Int]
    [Square s: Int]
  ]

  shape: [Circle r: 5]

  area: [match shape
    [Circle r]: [* 3 [* r r]]
    [Square s]: [* s s]
  ]
]
=== out
Dict({"Shape": Variant(Shape, Null), "Circle": Variant(Circle, Null), "Square": Variant(Square, Null), "shape": Variant(Circle, Int(5)), "area": Int(75)})

=== warn
arithmetic operator applied to non-numeric type `[]` at 16:17-16:24
